<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish unemployment rises to s/a 260,600 in March.</title>
<headline>Irish unemployment rises to s/a 260,600 in March.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of those claiming unemployment benefit rose to a seasonally adjusted 260,600 in March from 259,500 in February, Central Statistics Office (CSO) figures showed on Monday.  </p>
<p>But on an unadjusted basis, the numbers claiming benefit fell by 1,896 to 262,414 from 264,310 last month.</p>
<p>			Unadjusted	    Adjusted</p>
<p>Latest		 262,414		 260,600</p>
<p>Previous	     264,310		 259,500</p>
<p>Year-ago	     281,260		 279,400</p>
<p>(No percentages of the total workforce were given.)</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
